- Add more documentation
- Remove support for 32-bit architectures
- Remove hard coded sha256 PCR bank and NameAlg references from tpm2 package
- Add TPM_PT_NV_BUFFER_MAX to tpm2 capabilities info 
- Protected memory: rename the locked-memory primitive `pkg/memguard.Secret` to
  `MemoryEnclave` and migrate every in-repo caller. `Secret`, `New`,
  `NewFromString`, `NewRandom` and `MemoryEnclave.WithBytes` remain as
  deprecated aliases and are removed in the coordinated portfolio-wide
  protected-memory wave. See docs/security/protected-memory.md.
- Protected memory: hold PIV PINs and imported private key material in a
  `MemoryEnclave` across all five transports. `PIVGenerateRequest.PIN`,
  `PIVSignRequest.PIN`, `PIVImportRequest.PIN` and
  `PIVImportRequest.PrivateKeyPEM` are deprecated in favour of `PINEnclave` /
  `PrivateKey`, read through `WithPIN` / `WithPrivateKeyPEM`. The plain field
  is read only when no enclave was supplied; a destroyed enclave fails closed
  with `memguard.ErrDestroyed`. The wire contract is unchanged.
- REST (behaviour change, #665): a gRPC `FailedPrecondition` is now HTTP 409
  Conflict instead of 400, platform-wide, on both the web service and the
  daemon listener. 400 stays for `InvalidArgument` and `OutOfRange`. A REST
  caller that matched 400 for a refused state (a VM in the wrong state, a pool
  that still has allocations, a refused device lifecycle or service control
  call, an unbound attestation quote) now gets 409, which the SDK's REST
  transport reads as `AlreadyExists` instead of `InvalidArgument`. The writers
  that bypassed the shared mapping now answer 409 too: diskless boot on a
  connection with no TLS 1.3 exporter (`ErrBootChannelRequired`, was 400), the
  NAT64 module being unavailable (was 412), the KMS routes' `FailedPrecondition`
  (was 412), and the IDevID, IAK and AK key deletes, the IDevID and IAK
  certificate deletes with no TPM, and LDevID on the daemon listener (were
  412). The SDK's REST transport reads a 409 on a `DELETE`
  as `FailedPrecondition` (a delete cannot collide with an existing resource),
  so `idevid.ErrIdentityKeyNotDeletable` keeps its class; a 409 on any other
  method stays `AlreadyExists`. A 412 still reads as `FailedPrecondition`.
  gRPC, QUIC, MCP and the Unix socket are unchanged.
- BREAKING (gatewayd, #659): the `secret://` scheme is removed from gatewayd's
  secret-store references; use `kms://` (same path, same `?enc=` and
  `#<field>`). A `secret://` reference is now refused at service start with
  `secrets.ErrSchemeRemoved`, which wraps the SDK secret SPI's
  `InvalidSecretURIError` and names the `kms://` form. References resolve
  through the stack's canonical secret-resolution SPI (`ResolverRegistry`,
  re-exported by the go-quicbaas SDK) and fail closed. The NTP service's
  unresolved-NTS-material guard now refuses any `<scheme>://` value instead
  of a fixed scheme list.
